  <title id="bdl04regressioncost-title">Cost against mean square error for SMC and MLSMC on the TNN regression problem</title>
  <desc id="bdl04regressioncost-desc">Two log-log panels, cost from 100 to 1 million against MSE from about 0.00001 to 0.01. Left, smoothness s equal to 3: the MLSMC curve runs close to the MSE to the power minus 1 reference line, from a cost of about 250 at an MSE of 0.0075 to about 32,000 at 0.00004, while SMC rises more steeply to about 570,000 at the same MSE, roughly a factor of 10 to 20 above MLSMC. Right, s equal to 1.1: both methods rise from about 150 at an MSE of 0.008 to between 100,000 and 400,000 at 0.00005, with MLSMC only moderately below SMC. Thin curves above and below each line mark the credible intervals.</desc>
